<!--
  Commander Battle's Empire troop classes, merged into Native's mpclassdivisions.xml (MPClassDivisions, MultiplayerGame
  only). The rules are those of cb_mpclassdivisions_vlandia.xml; in short:
  - One class per weight of a formation class (role). The weight label comes from the multiplier bands per role
    (CommanderRoles.WeightBands). Horse archers have a single class, so no weight step.
  - The 7 stock Empire class ids are taken over in place (_replaceWhileMerging="true"), so they keep the stock index
    (MissionPeer.SelectedTroopIndex). A stock id's role comes only from its hero's default_group, so mp_skirmisher_empire
    is the light infantry here. The two further classes get new cb_ ids and are appended. Never put
    _replaceWhileMerging on a NEW id: with no id match the merger replaces the FIRST class of the file instead.
  - The only perk list (perk_list="1") is the weapon setups, in the order of the plan's culture variance table (the AI
    fields setup k for its k-th formation of a role). Index 0 is the class's own loadout; the others swap weapon slots
    with AlternativeEquipmentOnSpawn (target Any). No TroopCountOnSpawn: only the weight sets the count.
    game_mode="all". A setup the plan gives to medium and heavy only (the menavlion) is absent from the light class.
  - Empire doctrine: legion infantry with large kite shields on every weight, shielded archers, cataphracts. No
    two-handers besides the menavlion, one horse archer class, middling bows.
  - The menavlion is long and two-handed, so it carries no shield: an AlternativeEquipmentOnSpawn with a slot and no
    item empties the shield slot (Item1), and the sidearm stays in Item2.
  - Sidearm (Item2) rule: spears, the menavlion, lances and javelins keep the culture's sidearm, since they fight poorly
    up close. Sword setups clear it: their main weapon already is one.
  - Throwing weapons appear only in the skirmisher setups (foot and mounted): Imperial javelins, a bundle of 5 in Item0
    and 3 more in Item3, shield and sidearm kept. Not pila: mp_pilum is a TwoHandedPolearm craft whose thrown usage
    comes last, so it is wielded as a spear (X to switch), holds 1 per slot (Crafting: an alternative usage gets a
    stack of 1), can't be thrown mounted (polearm_thrown requires_no_mount) and RBM's skirmisher checks miss it. The
    Javelin-template items throw by default, from the saddle too.
  - The Empire's own lances (mp_empire_lance, mp_empire_heavy_lance) can't be couched: their handles are missing from
    the TwoHandedPolearm_Couchable weapon description. The lance setups use mp_western_lance, as the stock Cataphract.
  - A bad node makes the loader drop every later entry of this file silently; the CommanderBattle log lists the
    classes per culture when a mission opens.
  - Items only from Native's mpitems.xml (the only items multiplayer loads).
-->
